\section*{AB 2 Board Note \# 1}

Part (d)
\begin{itemize}
\item[] 3/3 Argument with the following three ingredients:
\begin{itemize}
\item[1.] The graph of \(y=b x e^{b x}\) is a horizontal compression or expansion (with a reflection across the \(y\)-axis if \(b<0\) ) of the graph of \(y=x e^{x}\).
\item[2.] The range of \(y=b x e^{b x}\) is therefore the same as the range of \(y=x e^{x}\).
\item[3.] Therefore the absolute minimum value of \(y=b x e^{b x}\) is the same for all (non-zero) values of \(b\).
\end{itemize}
\item[] 0/3 Analyzing the horizontal compression/expansion of graphs of \(y=b x e^{b x}\) for specific values of \(b\).
\end{itemize}
